### Version A - Durable Functions test scenarios
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Start the function host first:
###   func start
### Named requests (# @name) let later requests reference earlier responses,
### e.g. to poll status or grab an instanceId without copy/pasting manually.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 1: Valid expense under $100 -> Auto-approved
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario1
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Alice Chen",
  "employee_email": "alice@example.com",
  "amount": 45.50,
  "category": "supplies",
  "description": "Notebooks and pens",
  "manager_email": "manager@example.com"
}

### Poll status (wait a second, then run this - should show "approved")
GET {{scenario1.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 2: Valid expense >= $100, manager approves -> Approved
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario2
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Bob Singh",
  "employee_email": "bob@example.com",
  "amount": 350,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Flight to conference",
  "manager_email": "manager@example.com"
}

### Copy the instanceId from the scenario2 response below, then submit the
### manager's approval before the timer expires (default timeout: 1 minute)
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses/{{scenario2.response.body.id}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": true
}

### Poll status - should show "approved"
GET {{scenario2.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 3: Valid expense >= $100, manager rejects -> Rejected
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario3
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Carla Diaz",
  "employee_email": "carla@example.com",
  "amount": 899.99,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "Replacement laptop",
  "manager_email": "manager@example.com"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses/{{scenario3.response.body.id}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": false,
  "comment": "Please use the standard equipment refresh process instead"
}

### Poll status - should show "rejected"
GET {{scenario3.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 4: Valid expense >= $100, no manager response -> Escalated
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario4
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Dev Patel",
  "employee_email": "dev@example.com",
  "amount": 500,
  "category": "software",
  "description": "Annual IDE license",
  "manager_email": "manager@example.com"
}

### Do NOT submit a decision. Wait past MANAGER_TIMEOUT_MINUTES
### (1 minute by default), then poll - should show "escalated"
GET {{scenario4.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 5: Missing required fields -> Validation error
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario5
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Erin Wu",
  "amount": 60,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Team lunch"
}

### Poll status - should show "validation_error" (missing employee_email, manager_email)
GET {{scenario5.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenario 6: Invalid category -> Validation error
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scenario6
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Frank Lopez",
  "employee_email": "frank@example.com",
  "amount": 120,
  "category": "entertainment",
  "description": "Client dinner",
  "manager_email": "manager@example.com"
}

### Poll status - should show "validation_error" (invalid category)
GET {{scenario6.response.body.statusQueryGetUri}}
